  "result": "Perfect! All 453 tests pass (435 previous + 18 new dashboard tests).\n\n**Summary of dashboard implementation:**\n\n\u2705 **src/reports.js** \u2014 Added dashboard function:\n- `dashboard(invoices, asOf)` returns comprehensive invoice metrics:\n  - `counts`: Number of invoices per status (draft, issued, partially_paid, paid)\n  - `outstanding`: Total amount due on issued/partially_paid invoices\n  - `overdue`: { count, amount } of overdue invoices using overdueInvoices function\n  - `topCustomers`: Top 3 customers by total due amount, sorted descending\n\n\u2705 **test/reports.test.js** \u2014 18 comprehensive dashboard tests:\n- Object structure validation\n- Status counting (all statuses, empty array, single invoices)\n- Outstanding calculation (issued only, partially_paid only, mixed, excluding draft/paid)\n- Overdue metrics (with/without overdue invoices)\n- Top customers ranking (3 customers, less than 3, none, aggregating multiple invoices)\n- Multiple invoices per customer aggregation\n- Invalid date handling\n- Immutability (doesn't mutate inputs)\n- Edge cases (empty invoices, mixed statuses and overdue)\n\nKey features:\n- Aggregates customers with multiple invoices\n- Properly handles bulk discount in due amounts\n- Accounts for payments in outstanding calculation\n- Excludes draft and paid invoices from outstanding/top customers\n- Properly filters overdue invoices (issued/partially_paid only)\n- Returns up to 3 top customers sorted by highest due amount first",
